From: UniXNU contributors
Subject: [PATCH] k60: start only the authenticated physical battery source

The builtin archive inherits XNU's real IOPMPowerSource. It reads the actual
PMIC_RTR_ADSP_APPS protocol over exclusively leased SMEM/GLINK FIFOs and
publishes only after a valid coherent hardware sample. A missing PAS1 owner
handoff is logged and leaves battery status unavailable; no fixed percentage,
Android snapshot, live-DSP reset or safe-check bypass is introduced.

Parent integration must force-load libK60PhysicalBattery.a and define
XNU_K60_PHYSICAL_BATTERY=1 for IOKitBSDInit.cpo. No personality starts a fake
battery: the source registers only after its hardware validation.

--- a/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
+++ b/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
@@ -109,8 +109,16 @@
+#if defined(XNU_K60_PHYSICAL_BATTERY) && XNU_K60_PHYSICAL_BATTERY
+extern "C" void k60_physical_battery_start(void);
+#endif
+
 kern_return_t
 IOKitBSDInit( void )
 {
 	IOService::publishResource("IOBSD");
 
+#if defined(XNU_K60_PHYSICAL_BATTERY) && XNU_K60_PHYSICAL_BATTERY
+	k60_physical_battery_start();
+#endif
+
 #if IOPOLLED_COREFILE
 	corefile_open_call = thread_call_allocate_with_options(IOOpenPolledCoreFile, NULL, THREAD_CALL_PRIORITY_KERNEL, THREAD_CALL_OPTIONS_ONCE);
 #endif
